# Byte-exact fixtures.
#
# The repository sets core.autocrlf=input so that sheet files cannot acquire CRLF
# (preflight check 2). That same setting would silently rewrite these two fixtures
# on checkout, and both exist precisely to test byte-level form, so they must be
# stored exactly as written. Without -text the CRLF fixture loses its CRLF and
# E-L0-EOL stops firing on a fresh clone - a test that passes only on the machine
# that generated it.
tests/sweep/sheets/crlf.tsv -text
tests/sweep/sheets/enc.tsv -text

# Generated Rust is never committed (D6), but be explicit about the marker files
# too so a stray banner file is never normalised into looking legitimate.
docs/generated/** -text
